  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UN GRZ Joint Programme on GBV II</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">UN GRZ Joint Programme on GBV II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of the Republic of Zambia-United Nations Joint Programme on Gender Based Violence Phase II (GRZ-UN JPGBV Phase II) has applied to the Embassy for funding of 50 million SEK  to carry out the &quot;Strengthening Prevention and Response Services for GBV in Zambia Programme&quot; during the period 2019-2022.

The contribution aims to increase access to and use of quality prevention and response services for gender based violence in Zambia. This is by improving capacity to deliver coordinated GBV services; access to safe shelters; capacity to deliver quality legal services; economic empowerment of GBV survivors and improving multi-sectoral coordination and governance related to GBV in Zambia. 

The contribution is a follow up to phase I of the Government of the Republic of Zambia (GRZ)/United Nations joint programme on GBV. Phase II will again be jointly implemented by the GRZ through the Ministry of Gender and UN led by the United Nations Development Programme (UNDP), working with the United Nations Population Fund (UNFPA), United Nations Childrens Fund (UNICEF), International Organisation for Migration (IOM) and the International Labour Organisation (ILO). The contribution will cover fifteen districts of Zambia namely Kabwe, Kalumbila, Solwezi, Kasama, Mansa, Chinsali, Lundazi, Choma, Senanga, Chililabombwe, Lusaka, Itezhi Tezhi, Mumbwa, Mazabuka and Mongu.

The contribution&apos;s total budget is approximately 69 million SEK (USD 6,711,169). 50 million SEK (approximately USD 5,100,000) will be funded by Sweden and &#x20ac;1,490,000 (approximately USD 1,600,000) will be funded by Ireland.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Zambiska statens och FNs gemensamma program f&#xf6;r att bek&#xe4;mpa k&#xf6;nsbaserat v&#xe5;ld har ans&#xf6;kt om bidrag till genomf&#xf6;rande av programmets andra fas &#x201c;Strengthening Prevention and Response Services for GBV in Zambia Programme&quot; under perioden 2019-2022. 

Insatsen syftar till att &#xf6;ka tillg&#xe5;ng till och anv&#xe4;ndning av f&#xf6;rebyggande och v&#xe5;rdande tj&#xe4;nster relaterade till k&#xf6;nsbaserat v&#xe5;ld i Zambia. Detta ska ske genom att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra kapaciteten att p&#xe5; ett samordnat s&#xe4;tt leverera tj&#xe4;nster relaterade till k&#xf6;nsbaserat v&#xe5;ld, &#xf6;ka tillg&#xe5;ngen till skyddat boende, &#xf6;ka kapaciteten att bist&#xe5; med juridiska tj&#xe4;nster, &#xf6;ka &#xf6;verlevares eknomiska egenmakt och f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra den multi-sektoriella samordningen och f&#xf6;rvaltningen relaterad till k&#xf6;nsbaserat v&#xe5;ld i Zambia.

Insatsen &#xe4;r en uppf&#xf6;ljning av fas 1 av zambiska statens och FNs gemensamma program f&#xf6;r att bek&#xe4;mpa k&#xf6;nsbaserat v&#xe5;ld. Fas II kommer &#xe5;terigen att genomf&#xf6;ras av zambiska staten, genom ministeriet f&#xf6;r j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet, och FN genom FNs utvecklingsprogram, UNDP I samarbete med FNs befolkningsfond UNFPA, FNs barnfond UNICEF, FNs migrationsorganisation IOM och den internationella arbetsorganisationen ILO. Insatsen t&#xe4;cker femton zambiska distrikt: Kabwe, Kalumbila, Solwezi, Kasama, Mansa, Chinsali, Lundazi, Choma, Senanga, Chililabombwe, Lusaka, Itezhi Tezhi, Mumbwa, Mazabuka and Mongu.

Insatsens totala budget &#xe4;r ca 69 MSEK (USD 6,711,169), d&#xe4;r Sverige bidrar med 50 MSEK (ca 5 100 000 USD) och Irland med &#x20ac;1,490,000 (ca 1 600 000 USD eller ca 19 MSEK).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To contribute to strengthening GBV prevention and response systems in Zambia in line with the provisions of the Anti-Gender Based Violence Act.</narrative>
  </description>
